    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.21_ologs_and_typed_english.chapters.01_olog_as_typed_english.sections.01_olog_definition_spivak_kent.concrete_anchor_1_O_eng#ologcategoryoeng" .
silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_01_olog_as_typed_english_sections_01_olog_definition_spivak_kent_concrete_anchor_1_O_eng#ologcategoryoeng silm:hasLongDescription "The OlogCategoryOEng is the typed-English olog category presented by paper 21 (boxes = a domestic cat, a body mass quality, ...; arrows = has as body mass, is measured by, ...). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'O_eng', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
